  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1980s, John Brandenburg, a scientist who argues that life on Mars was destroyed by a nuclear war, says he sent pictures to the astronomer Carl Sagan. When he later asked Sagan what he thought of them, Sagan answered, \"I never got them.\" Brandenburg tells this to Michels as something that happened to him, a hint that the material may have been stopped along the way."
